{
  "$comment": [
    "Router v0's labelled set (#11460): requests to Coder, each with the judgment a correct System One gives (`label`, the `route-v1` questions read by argmax) and the harness and policy step a correct router picks (`expect`).",
    "`situation` changes the default situation: Claude Code and the Coder loop both admitted, neither preferred, no plan window reported, cost and speed balanced. `claude: false` leaves Claude Code out (signed out), `five_hour` is the plan window's used percent, `prefer` puts a harness first by the person's routing preferences, `cost` and `speed` are the sliders (1 to 5).",
    "`judged` holds the probabilities the gateway door (Clef-Flash on the H100) gave for the row, recorded by the ignored live test with ROUTER_RECORD set; the unit test replays them through the policy with no network.",
    "No row is picked by matching its words: every expectation follows from the judgment and the situation through route-policy-v1."
  ],
  "schema": "openagents.coder.route.labeled.v1",
  "set": "route-v1",
  "policy": "route-policy-v1",
